From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: EE Cycle Rate goes down to -6 (27%) for the user to choose

ARMSX2 stops the EE cycle rate at -3, as PCSX2 does. On an RG52 Mini lower
rates help the heaviest games: at -5 God of War's own time runs 34-39% faster
than at -3 (emulated vsyncs a second) at the same frames a second, and Jak and
Daxter's intro draws 23% more frames, 17% faster (dArkOS docs/TODO.md, "PS2:
EE cycle rate below -3"). Nobody has checked them for breakage, so they are
offered, not set: our default stays -3, and the settings menu lists 36%, 31%
and 27% Speed below 50% (-4, -5, -6; the arm64 recompiler charges a block
(5 - 2 * (rate + 1)) / 32 of its cycles where the default charges 4/32).

VU0's micro programs are charged the same ratio (they kept 100% at -4..-6
otherwise, as an unknown rate). The governor (DynamicEECycleRate, which
AutoTune can turn on) still lowers the rate to -3 at most, as before; a rate
set below that is its own floor.

diff --git a/pcsx2/Config.h b/pcsx2/Config.h
index b3025abd..129cdb35 100644
--- a/pcsx2/Config.h
+++ b/pcsx2/Config.h
@@ -1401,7 +1401,10 @@ struct Pcsx2Config
 	// ------------------------------------------------------------------------
 	struct SpeedhackOptions
 	{
-		static constexpr s8 MIN_EE_CYCLE_RATE = -3;
+		// dArkOS: down to -6 (the EE at 36%, 31%, 27% for -4, -5, -6), for the user to choose.
+		// The governor still lowers the rate to -3 at most, as before.
+		static constexpr s8 MIN_EE_CYCLE_RATE = -6;
+		static constexpr s8 MIN_EE_CYCLE_RATE_GOVERNOR = -3;
 		static constexpr s8 MAX_EE_CYCLE_RATE = 3;
 		static constexpr u8 MAX_EE_CYCLE_SKIP = 3;
 
diff --git a/pcsx2/EECycleRate.cpp b/pcsx2/EECycleRate.cpp
index 374b2861..6d418d4f 100644
--- a/pcsx2/EECycleRate.cpp
+++ b/pcsx2/EECycleRate.cpp
@@ -37,7 +37,9 @@ namespace
 {
 	s8 FloorFor(s8 configured)
 	{
-		return static_cast<s8>(std::max<int>(Pcsx2Config::SpeedhackOptions::MIN_EE_CYCLE_RATE, configured - 2));
+		// dArkOS: the governor stops at -3 as before; a rate configured below it is its own floor.
+		return static_cast<s8>(std::min<int>(configured,
